// This file intentionally does not parse: the grammar's Integer range
// validator only accepts signed-integer literals (range=[lower,upper]), so
// a decimal lower bound such as 0.5 is a ParseException, never a semantic
// one. Reaching the intended rule -- a float bound on an Integer property
// -- needs a hand-authored JSON AST, since no valid CTO text attaches a
// non-integer lower/upper bound to an IntegerDomainValidator. See
// number_validator_003_invalid_range_type.json. NOTE: as authored, current
// concerto-core (v5.x) does not actually reject this: NumberValidator
// stores lower/upper as plain numbers with no check that they are integers
// for an Integer-typed field, so no error is thrown for it (see the
// scenario in scalars.feature, and the P5-08a report).
namespace org.concerto.scalars.valid.num003@1.0.0

concept InvalidInteger {
  o Integer value range=[0.5, 100]
}
